    "segments": [
     {
      "start": 1915,
      "end": 1953,
      "headway_min": 240,
      "note": "The B&O began operating the FM&P in March 1915 and absorbed it as the FM&P Branch, later the FM&P Subdivision of its Pittsburgh Division. Morgantown's B&O trains ran from here to Fairmont, where they met the main stem. Passenger service ended 25 September 1953; B&O train 66, the last passenger train through Morgantown, ran on Saturday 21 September 1953. Freight continued until a December 1990 landslide, after which the Fairmont - Morgantown line was abandoned in January 1991 and became the Mon River Trail. Frequency estimated, unsourced.",
